<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>



<<~ ahu #/the-record-laws>>

!! The record laws ~ what a command IS, and where a name lives

Two laws the door has always obeyed and no carrier has stated.

!!! Records, not RPC

''A command rides as an intent RECORD; an outcome rides as a receipt RECORD.'' Neither reads as a remote
call. Each record flows through the admin surface as a ''local-first artifact'' — authored, addressed,
and readable after the fact by anything that can read a tiddler. A temporary record stays acceptable where
the flow needs only a short life; a call that leaves no record does not.

''What the law buys:'' an RPC leaves a trace only where someone logged one, and the log answers to a
different grammar than the call. A record IS the trace, in the grammar everything else already reads.

!!! The `lar:` locality law

''Every system `id` uses the `lar:` URI scheme'' — command ids, receipt ids, audience ids, principal ids,
session artifact ids, storage artifact ids, and any other first-class name.

''The authority says who spoke; the naming CONVENTION reads as a courtesy, never a verdict:''

<<~ scale locality """hostless ~ "`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/commands/promote/…`" — a hot, warm or cold STORAGE artifact, on-disk projections first -> hostful ~ "`lar://node.alpha.local/ha.ka.ba/bags/sessions/live/…`" — a LIVE session artifact, named at the node holding it""">>

''An author following the convention hands a reader a hint, and the law stops there.'' Hostful and hostless
name WHAT a URI names — a hostful authority states who spoke, under what grant, from where, which reads as
a fact about the CONTENT and keeps holding for as long as the content stands
(`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary#/the-promotion-boundary`).

⚠ ''So a reader derives no durability from the form, and MUST NOT.'' Durability answers to the holding bag
and the layer, never to the count of slashes: a captured session turn promoted into canon carries its
hostful name onward and outlives every node that ever held it. A caller that gates, routes, or ranks on
the address form reads a content property as a layer property — the failure this law names.

''Provenance:'' harvested verbatim from `lar:///lares_research/research-streams/lararium/LARES-CLI-DAEMON-SPRINT-PLAN`,
where both laws stood settled with no live carrier holding either.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-law>>

! The Vessel Door ~ one namespace over the vessel's island

''ONE NAMESPACE PER CAUSAL ISLAND; THE PLANE RIDES AS A PARAMETER, NEVER A NEW VERB.'' That law governs
this CLI: the sensorium surface answers at two doors — one sovereign, one guest — and no legacy alias
answers anywhere.

''The vessel is a causal island and speaks through ONE name.'' Its store, its genesis artifact, its
daemon and its corpus form one island by every test this house applies, so they answer at one door. ''A
plane with no door has nowhere to put new capability but the top level'' — which is why the verb count
grows back wherever the law has not reached, and where to look when it does.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-primitives>>

!! What the door answers — four primitives and one read

Every substrate motion in this CLI composes from these, and no composition earns a primitive's seat.

<<~ has Primitive found "mints the vessel identity, the persona root, the social planes and the bootstrap ~ idempotent, skips what stands">>
<<~ has Primitive stand "brings the daemon up, foreground or detached, and reports what it found ~ attach when one already answers">>
<<~ has Primitive stop "ends a running daemon by port, signals gracefully and waits for its exit ~ never a restart in disguise">>
<<~ has Primitive seed "plants every bags holding back into its doc, kind-routed, diff-gated ~ idempotent; a converged tree no-ops">>

''The read beside them'': `read` — the pure inspection that starts nothing (bootstrap
presence, storage size, port, seal state, personas, quorum).

`build` compiles the workspace and stamps its source digest inside `rite refresh`; it names no vessel door.
`stand` carries `--foreground`, `--with-web`, `--restart`, `--observe`, `--install`, `--init`, and `--admit <file>` postures. The sub-doors `card`, `wire`, and `rite` print the ContactCard, point machine AI surfaces at the vessel, and run the named compositions.

''RE-DERIVING THE GENESIS ISLAND IS NOT A DOOR.'' Advancing the composition (the engine, the memetic-wikitext
grammar) is a MESH act that goes out past a single vessel — it rides `nexus kahuli`, the engine/grammar
ratchet. The LOCAL re-derive rides only as an internal step of the `rebuild` rite and the
`build:genesis` build script; other plugins ride
separately as `@cad` caps rather than folding into the grammar ratchet.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-collapse>>

!! The collapse, verb by verb

Each row names a RETIRED TOP-LEVEL spelling (`lares <name>`) and the vessel door or rite that carries its motion. ''No aliases survive'' — a name
that still answers teaches that both spellings stand, and the surface regrows from there. Every spelling
below refuses with `unknown command`, flags included: routing an unknown name to the global help would
return 0 and print a full page, which reads exactly like a door that opened.

''NO DOOR WIPES.'' Three retired spellings named a wipe of the vessel store, and no door or rite answers one
(operator-ruled): a fresh start runs by hand, moving the old homes aside
(<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/fresh-start">>).

|! retired |! composes |! answers at |
| `init` | found | `vessel found` |
| `wake` | found? · stand · read | `vessel stand` (the entry point; keeps its report) |
| `serve` | stand (foreground) | `vessel stand --foreground` |
| `dev` | stand · vite | `vessel stand --with-web` |
| `stop` | stop | `vessel stop` |
| `reset` | wipe · found | no door — a fresh start runs by hand |
| `fresh` | wipe · stand | no door — a fresh start runs by hand |
| `reconcile` | stop · stand | `vessel stand --restart` |
| `refresh` | build · stop · stand | `vessel rite refresh` |
| `rebuild` | re-derive · stand | `vessel rite rebuild` |
| `build-genesis` · `bake` | the internal re-derive, or the mesh overturn | internal step: `vessel rite rebuild` · `nexus kahuli` |
| `regenesis` | stop · wipe · re-derive · stand · seed | no door — a fresh start runs by hand |
| `seed` | seed | `vessel seed` |
| `status` · `node status` | read | `vessel read` |

''THE COMPOSITIONS RIDE AS RITES, NEVER VERBS.'' The rite door carries `founding`, `refresh`, and
`rebuild` as named compositions over the primitives. A composition earns a pet-name; it gains no top-level name.

''The test for a rite versus a primitive'': a primitive names one motion
and cannot be expressed as a sequence of the others. Everything else composes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-founding-rite>>

!! The founding rite rides the rite-door

''The founding rite composes: found · stand · seed.'' No stop and no second bake — a movement that stopped
the daemon and re-baked genesis would tear down what the second movement built moments earlier. The only
part a founding needs there is the seeding.

''A RITE THAT NEVER RESTARTS NEVER CROSSES THE SEAL GATE.'' Sealing the vault writes a marker, so every later
daemon boot wants the passphrase in its environment. A movement that RESTARTS the daemon crosses that gate —
and an operator who sealed by typing would carry the passphrase forward by hand between two movements or
watch the vessel come up at the floor. The founding rite restarts nothing, so no carry-forward step exists
to get wrong.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-ripples>>

!! Every caller that closes with the door

''A door that leaves callers on old names has collapsed nothing.'' These surfaces name substrate verbs
directly, so each moves in the same act as any change to the door — and each row below names what keeps it
moved.

# ''THE GENERATED MCP MIRROR.'' The CLI↔MCP↔seat isomorphism rides a GENERATED fixture, never a
  hand-edited one. Rebuild the CLI first, then regenerate. A hand-edit here reads as a passing test over a
  surface nobody generated — and so does a fixture nobody regenerated, which is why the weld rides a
  witness (#/the-verifications) rather than a habit.
# ''THE FRESH-BUILD GATE.'' Membership DERIVES from the door rather than from a remembered list of verb
  names. A roster drifts the moment a surface changes — the very defect this door closes. The derived
  test states its EXCEPTIONS instead, so it fails safe: a sub-door added later stays gated until someone
  argues it out.
# ''THE FOUNDING RUNBOOK.'' It instructs substrate verbs directly, and as the operator-instruction source a
  stale command there fails at the worst moment a command can fail. `tools/rite-commands-witness.sh` reads
  each instructed command at its dispatch position.
# ''THE REHEARSAL HARNESS.'' `tools/rehearse-founding.sh` walks the rite by name; its preflight, its founding
  step and its seed step all name the door.
# ''THE CONTAINER BOOT + THE WITNESS SCRIPTS.'' They found and stand vessels by verb name.
# ''THE SESSION-START HOOK.'' It calls the entry point with the observe capability. The capability must
  survive the rename intact — a hook that gains the standing capability by accident turns looking into
  acting.
# ''EVERY HANDLER'S OWN HEADER.'' A handler whose docstring self-names a retired spelling carries cosmetic
  residue; sweep it in the same pass as the name.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/what-stands>>

!! What stays outside the vessel door, and why

''NOT the noun-doors.'' `nexus`, `persona`, `vault`, `library`, `circle`, `cabal`, `hooks`, `sense`,
`mempalace`, `sensorium` already obey the law. Touching them spends risk for nothing.

''NOT the content verbs.'' `bag`, `wiki`, `ingest`, `act`, `edge`, `draft`, `normalize`, `repack` name the
corpus island rather than the vessel island. They may want their own door one day; that is a separate
reading and it does not belong in this act.

''NOT the identity verbs.'' `device-admit` and `raise` name ceremonies between vessels, not motions of
one vessel's substrate. ''An OWED capability carries no door at all'' — the Nexus invite ceremony rides
no verb until its transport lands, the same way `cabal feed` stands built and unspelled.

''A RENAME MOVES NAMES AND NOTHING ELSE.'' A change that moves a name and a behaviour together cannot get
verified — a green suite afterward proves neither half.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-verifications>>

!! What proves the door holds

''Each of these fails loudly on a half-moved door'', and each rides a witness rather than a hand —
because a verification an operator has to remember to run is a verification that reports on their memory.

# ''The tree typechecks'' — `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`. A green build has not typechecked: the compiler
  colorizes, so a reader grepping for the word `error` and its code matches nothing while a package
  carries dozens. The witness reads per package and exits non-zero on any real error.
# ''The mirror names the table the CLI carries'' — `tools/mirror-parity-witness.sh`. The generated
  isomorphism fixture goes stale by NOT being regenerated, and the checks standing around it cannot see
  that: the three-way guard asserts the fixture's own internal coherence (which staleness satisfies), and
  the projection test compares live to live. ''Nothing else welds the fixture to the table.''
# ''No old name answers.'' Every retired top-level spelling MUST fail as an unknown command, ''with or without `--help`''.
  A surviving alias names the failure mode this door exists to prevent, and it hides perfectly behind a
  passing suite.
# ''The surface gets measured at the VERB, never at the door.'' A door count reports a collapse the
  operator cannot feel: the fan-out lives one level below the number, so a surface that reads halved by
  doors may not have moved at all. Both figures DERIVE, printed on every rite-commands run — ''the pair is
  the reading, either alone flatters'', and a figure transcribed into prose ages silently.
# ''The rehearsal walks its cycles green'' (`tools/rehearse-founding.sh`) — which also proves the founding
  rite composes correctly, since the harness performs the rite rather than describing it.
# ''The founding runbook reads end to end'' (`tools/rite-commands-witness.sh`), every instructed sub-door resolving at a DISPATCH POSITION. A
  substring test reads the vocabulary of a file rather than its dispatch, and passes on the very line that
  disproves it — `case "contract": … cmdContract(args, "admit")` waved a rite instructing `nexus admit`
  straight through. A rite amended by many hands drifts fastest at exactly the commands nobody re-typed.

<<~/ahu>>

